<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Triphylia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Triphylia was a region of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> between the rivers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpheios">Alpheios</a> and Neda, south of Elis, with towns such as Lepreon and Samikon. Long dominated by Elis, it was detached from Elean control by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> after their war of about 402–400 BCE and later joined the Arcadian League. It lies today in the regional unit of Elis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/triphylia.jpg" alt="Triphylia" width="320" height="626" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Jolle~commonswiki · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regi%C3%B3nDe%C3%89lide.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
